  "query_preview": "../Friday through Sunday/... \nBenign days are ahead compared to the last week of strong systems\nfor the panhandle. Friday sees the low pressure currently in the \nnorthern gulf finally fill completely, with another system moving \nup from the southwest. Not expecting this system to reach the \nsouthern panhandle fully, only expecting the extreme southern \nportion to be clipped by some moisture Saturday going into Sunday.\nOtherwise, expect to start out with mostly a cool trend, with \novernight temperatures dipping down into the low to mid 30s, and \nthe northern panhandle possibly getting down into the upper 20s. \nCould see some northerly winds increase out of Lynn Canal, but \nuncertainty in low strength and has lead to less winds for now.",
